@SecureApi_HostAddress = http://localhost:8080
@AccessToken = PEGUE_AQUI_SU_ACCESS_TOKEN

### Obtener un access token local. Copie accessToken en la variable anterior.
POST {{SecureApi_HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "Alice123!"
}

###

### Sin JWT: debe responder 401 Unauthorized.
GET {{SecureApi_HostAddress}}/api/v1/documents/secure/1
Accept: application/json

###

### Ver la identidad extraída del JWT: debe responder usr_alice.
GET {{SecureApi_HostAddress}}/api/v1/documents/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{AccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### Control BOLA mitigado: 200 si el propietario coincide.
GET {{SecureApi_HostAddress}}/api/v1/documents/secure/1
Authorization: Bearer {{AccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### Control BOLA mitigado: 403 si el documento pertenece a otro usuario.
GET {{SecureApi_HostAddress}}/api/v1/documents/secure/2
Authorization: Bearer {{AccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### BOLA intencional: permite consultar otro documento con un JWT válido.
GET {{SecureApi_HostAddress}}/api/v1/documents/vulnerable/2
Authorization: Bearer {{AccessToken}}
Accept: application/json
